Description: python-common: add ceph.cryptotools (backport from Tentacle)
 With a Rust (PyO3) based python3-bcrypt or python3-cryptography, as in
 Debian trixie/forky and Ubuntu 26.04, these modules can only be loaded into
 one Python interpreter per process. ceph-mgr runs every module in an
 interpreter of its own, so in Squid all mgr modules after the first fail to
 load ("PyO3 modules do not yet support subinterpreters"), the dashboard among
 them. Tentacle solves this with ceph.cryptotools, which runs the crypto
 functions of the mgr in a child process ("python3 -m
 ceph.cryptotools.cryptotools"). This adds the package unchanged from Tentacle
 20.2.5 (https://github.com/ceph/ceph/pull/66794 and #69446), except for a
 comment in __init__.py, which a patch can't create empty. The next patches
 make the mgr use it.
